{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal","id":1450874,"title":"Show me a Heroic Abyssal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-03T13:24:33-07:00","id":1450874,"title":"Show me a Heroic Abyssal","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> After reading the new excerpt of essence and checking all the exalts, I'm in need of guidance. I can see the heroic and villainous angle of every type of exalt except one: the Abyssals. Unless I'm missing something from their description, they are basically agents of death and enemies of life. Now, I have to admit that my knowledge of Abyssals comes from this excerpt and what I've seen in the wiki, so I may be missing something. That's why I wanted to ask you all if you could show me how you would make a heroic Abyssal, what are their redeeming qualities?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-03-2021, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T14:11:24-07:00","id":1450883,"title":"","content":"Well, the &quot;classic&quot; heroic Abyssal, which XS only mentions in passing, is a tormented renegade from the Deathlords' cause, his Exaltation a terrible burden, his goal redemption.<br /> <br /> Late in its run, though, 2e presented some divergences from that dualistic morality of loyalist/renegade, which 3e will hopefully enable. Some examples from that time:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Speaker for the Dead</b><br /> He lives in a cave high on the mountain, overlooking the shadowland. One day every week he meditates in the graveyard, watching the living venerate the dead. Those whose offerings are meager he investigates. If he finds them misers, he makes them into the paupers their offerings suggest them to be. If they are too poor to properly venerate their ancestors, he helps increase their fortunes in the world as best he can.<br /> When Immaculate monks came to ward shut the shadowland with prayers and salt and road-shrines to greedy gods, he scattered them with his fists. When he found a child wandering lost on the north road, he led her home. When an agent of the Deathlords arrived, preaching the doctrine of Oblivion, he sent that man to experience his black apotheosis firsthand.<br /> He walks among the dead by night, settling disputes among households top-heavy with elders. He distills the wisdom of the ancestors into words that ring true to those too young or alive to heed those who came before. He punishes those ghosts that grow fat on worship without guiding or assisting the living.<br /> He wears a mask of beautiful ivory and robes of the finest silk. No one has ever seen his face. Maggots writhe in his footprints. He speaks for the dead. Pity those who will not listen.<br /> <br /> <b>The Wrath of Heaven</b><br /> The Lunar cast auguries for her mate and found the stars silent. But she didn\u2019t give up. She finally found him on the road leading away from Chiaroscuro, riding a black horse, devoid of purpose, another ghost blowing across the desert.<br /> Now their love gives them both meaning. She is Chosen of the Argent Madonna, the clever eyes and fingers of Heaven. He is her blade. Descending into the Underworld, they destroyed a column of the Legion Sanguinary. Returning to the living world, they laid siege to a blasphemous ziggurat amidst silver sands. When the Wyld Hunt sent its assassins, he stood strong and protected her. When her mentor told her this was not as her mate should be, she laughed.<br /> They go up and down the length of the desert, the black rider and the little bat flying ahead of him. Their legend spreads. The wicked fear their coming. The just doubt they are real. The dead search for them both. Ten thousand terrible things lurk among the sands of two worlds. None of them are safe.<br /> <br /> <b>The Pale Evangelist</b><br /> To all suffering, he says, there is an answer.<br /> All who\u2019ve seen the pale evangelist remember him. His lips are red as blood. His skin is alabaster. He wears carnations in his hair. He is finer and more beautiful than the world through which he moves. He awes the dead and disquiets the living.<br /> The evangelist walks the lands of the living to spread the good news of the grave. There is a joy in him as he describes the beauty of the Underworld, the passion of the dead, the magnificence of eternity. A paper shirt burned in honor of the dead, he says, will become a fine silk tunic, a tiny wooden sword a mighty blade. The dead do not starve. They do not freeze. So long as the living honor them, they want for nothing.<br /> Ancestor cults spring up in his wake. He assists suicides, smiling as he guides those with the courage to heed his words into a new existence, free of the indignities of flesh. The pale evangelist believes it is better to be dead than to be alive, and many find his testimony convincing.<br /> Of course, preaching anything inconvenient to the powers of the world has its dangers. The Wyld Hunt seeks his whereabouts. Gods confront him, incensed by his accusations of venal extortion. At these times he summons up the corpses of the departed to fight on his behalf; it amuses him to make the detritus of life serve the cause of death.<br /> <br /> <b>The Blade of Vengeance</b><br /> The dead have grievances. She settles them.<br /> She frequently targets the Guild, leading some to believe she took the Last Breath in chains. Her blades strike down tyrannical ghosts, reunites murderers with their victims, permanently still the tongues of necromancers.<br /> She shrouds herself in dark winding-cloth and carries a short daiklave on each hip. Rumor has it she is beautiful beneath her shrouds, but no one can claim to have seen anything but her red eyes. She rarely speaks, and then only to set terms and demand payment. Her prices vary: five thousand obols to slay a wicked king; a relic dagger to burn down a Guildsman\u2019s manor; a gold brooch to slay a father who drowned his five daughters.<br /> She will not act as the agent of those with power enough to take their own revenge. Those who attempt to deceive her regret it\u2014briefly. She believes Creation unjust and the Underworld a house of suffering. Whenever she helps a ghost pass on to Lethe, its business fulfilled, she feels the rage burning in her own heart cool ever so slightly. Perhaps that fire will never go out. It matters little. The Underworld is vast. </div> </div> </div> Most of these, you can even do as a servant of the Deathlords. You just have to accept that your boss is a dolorous and black-hearted tyrant of the dead.<br /> But that's awesome, so, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 06-03-2021, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T14:42:21-07:00","id":1450884,"title":"","content":"Wow, thank you so much. These examples are awesome! They give so much more context a nuance to the Abyssals. Now I have examples to show my players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T16:07:29-07:00","id":1450888,"title":"","content":"There's &quot;going around killing everybody&quot; enemy of life and there's &quot;be all gothy and melodramatic and composing elaborate poetry about the fragility of fallen foes&quot; enemy of life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T23:02:59-07:00","id":1450914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal#post1450874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> After reading the new excerpt of essence and checking all the exalts, I'm in need of guidance. I can see the heroic and villainous angle of every type of exalt except one: the Abyssals. Unless I'm missing something from their description, they are basically agents of death and enemies of life. Now, I have to admit that my knowledge of Abyssals comes from this excerpt and what I've seen in the wiki, so I may be missing something. That's why I wanted to ask you all if you could show me how you would make a heroic Abyssal, what are their redeeming qualities?<br /> <br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>Midnight Therapist.<br /> <br /> I'm serious. Their Active Anima makes them perfect grief counselors, since they can inspire inner peace or acceptance just as easily as terror or despair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T01:06:29-07:00","id":1450923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450888#post1450888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's &quot;going around killing everybody&quot; enemy of life and there's &quot;be all gothy and melodramatic and composing elaborate poetry about the fragility of fallen foes&quot; enemy of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't know which one I despise most XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T01:10:39-07:00","id":1450924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450914#post1450914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Midnight Therapist.<br /> <br /> I'm serious. Their Active Anima makes them perfect grief counselors, since they can inspire inner peace or acceptance just as easily as terror or despair.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hum...an interesting concept. I suppose their relationship with death and abilities makes them uniquely qualified to offer people a new perspective. They bring inner peace to the living by helping them understand death and life. <br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T03:31:33-07:00","id":1450940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450923#post1450923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I don't know which one I despise most XD</div> </div> </div> </div>I think something that Abyssals and Infernals are primed to explore is how not everything people will sincerely cheer for is good or healthy.<br /> <br /> Like, if impoverishing people for not making sufficient grave offerings, assisting suicides, and acting as an assassination service for vengeful ghosts are appropriately heroic, I think you and I and the books are basically on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T04:45:47-07:00","id":1450943,"title":"","content":"you want to see a heroic abyssal? ok<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://bloody-disgusting.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Hellsing-2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T05:23:34-07:00","id":1450947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450940#post1450940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think something that Abyssals and Infernals are primed to explore is how not everything people will sincerely cheer for is good or healthy.<br /> <br /> Like, if impoverishing people for not making sufficient grave offerings, assisting suicides, and acting as an assassination service for vengeful ghosts are appropriately heroic, I think you and I and the books are basically on the same page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see how Abyssals and Infernals would develop a very twisted sense of morality that nevertheless makes perfect sense for them, as you say it could be an interesting concept to explore.<br /> I admit that the very concept of heroic can be very ambiguous, what is heroic for someone is villainous to others, I should have been more specific. The issue I had is that I didn't see any redeeming quality in them, at least till you all gave me examples.<br /> I wasn't so much interested in seeing a &quot;heroic&quot; abyssal in the classic sense as seeing how you would play a &quot;moral&quot; abyssal (regardless of how twisted that moral is) that wants more than the destruction of life and veneration of death, or approaches these principles with more nuance. <br /> In any case, you gave me great ideas. Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T05:26:42-07:00","id":1450948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450943#post1450943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you want to see a heroic abyssal? ok<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://bloody-disgusting.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Hellsing-2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> +1 for Hellsing reference.<br /> <br /> Now seriously, I don't know if I would call him &quot;heroic&quot;, but I can see him as the perfect example of an antihero Abyssal monster that hunts other monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T05:44:13-07:00","id":1450950,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I honestly see him {the above picture of Alucard from the VanHelsing anime} as an Abyssal- other then him being a vampire - he was is more a Infernal [or maybe a Coruptued Lunar] to be.<br /> <br /> but I could be a hypocrite as I was going to suggest that Netflix Castlevaina has a few people who could be Heroic Abyssals - Issac for one ... for reason that are spoilery","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":324,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","user":"ardenty","date":". 06-04-2021, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar324_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T13:22:06-07:00","id":1450978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450940#post1450940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think something that Abyssals and Infernals are primed to explore is how not everything people will sincerely cheer for is good or healthy.<br /> <br /> Like, if impoverishing people for not making sufficient grave offerings, assisting suicides, and acting as an assassination service for vengeful ghosts are appropriately heroic, I think you and I and the books are basically on the same page.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> #1: As described it was heroic, he made sure the ghosts gave their descendants aid so anyone that was shorting them out of greed was actively ripping off their own family despite services rendered. He didn't punish the poor who couldn't afford it, just the greedy who ripped off their own flesh and blood.<br /> <br /> #2: Nah, that guy is a creeper who needs to go kill himself first if suicide is so damn great.<br /> <br /> #3 Depends on the grievance, taking a job from the ghost of a guild factor who wants you to kill those uppity slaves that revolted and put his head on a pike is a bit different from taking a job from a slave who wants his master killed for beating them to death in a fit of pique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 06-04-2021, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T13:56:01-07:00","id":1450981,"title":"","content":"Would Guts from the Manga &quot;Berserk&quot; count as a Heroic Abyssal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T14:08:12-07:00","id":1450984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450981#post1450981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Guts from the Manga &quot;Berserk&quot; count as a Heroic Abyssal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably depends on what part of the story Guts you are talking about, he was a pretty big prick for awhile there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T14:55:06-07:00","id":1450989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450981#post1450981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Guts from the Manga &quot;Berserk&quot; count as a Heroic Abyssal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hum...maybe. It could fit in both Infernal and Abyssal categories. I'm inclined more towards Infernal due to his background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T19:38:53-07:00","id":1451002,"title":"","content":"Work for the Silver Prince and promote death as just another step on the social ladder. EZ","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T04:11:10-07:00","id":1451036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450978#post1450978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just the greedy who ripped off their own flesh and blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, we find how the definition of a heroic character is fluid not just in the standards applied to their behaviour, but in differing perspectives on people around them.<br /> <br /> It can create interesting conflicts to pit the Abyssal who says that it's greed to not give some of your possessions to a ghost relative, the Immaculate who says that it's greed to <i>be</i> a ghost relative and expect offerings, and the other observer who think that the existence of both sides is valid but neither is innately entitled to anything from the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">#2: Nah, that guy is a creeper who needs to go kill himself first if suicide is so damn great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Abyssal to ghost is an unambiguous downgrade, but characters could plausibly form beliefs that mortal to ghost is an upgrade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T04:30:49-07:00","id":1451039,"title":"","content":"Do people here mean \u201cHeroic\u201d as in \u201cRescuing kitten from the tree and punch evil alien\u201d type of heroic, or \u201cMy PC rape and pillage half the universe and yours is next\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T06:22:09-07:00","id":1451045,"title":"","content":"Abyssals, as the Exalted of Death, tend more towards being anti-heroes than what we traditionally think of as heroes. In Marvel terms they'd be more likely to be Punisher than Captain America. But in the more classical and epic sense of the term Hero, an Abyssal could certainly qualify.<br /> <br /> That said you could certainly have an Abyssal who has the same story arc as any other Exalted and engages in similar heroics, protecting people, saving Creation, etc. An Abyssal would be more likely to be a protector, defender and nurturer of the Underworld and the ghosts that exist within it than the living, but even so it is by no means impossible for an Abyssal to serve as a protector for Creation and the people who live within it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T06:35:29-07:00","id":1451047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450978#post1450978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#2: Nah, that guy is a creeper who needs to go kill himself first if suicide is so damn great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean for many mortals in Creation being a ghost might be better than being alive. As a ghost you don't have to worry about starving to death, you don't have to worry about disease, you don't have to worry about droughts or natural disasters. You don't have to worry about getting older. You don't have to worry about dying. You don't have to worry about the people you care for dying. If you're a ghost you can spend eternity with your loved ones, largely free from pain or worries. In many respects, existing as a ghost (immortal, free from the pains of life, surrounded forever by the people you love) is not so different from the concept of Heaven that quite a few real-world religions preach about.<br /> <br /> To the the starving, the destitute, the diseased, the crippled, etc, the Underworld could look like a pretty attractive alternative than the continual suffering they experience daily in Creation. And of course, people could take the long-term view - if you're only going to live for 40 or 50 years and then exist as a ghost for half a million years after that, why feel too attached to those mere 50 years, especially if they mostly suck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T07:49:55-07:00","id":1451050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451047#post1451047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean for many mortals in Creation being a ghost might be better than being alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, provided you knew <b>for a fact</b> that you'd actually <i>get to be</i> a ghost, <i>and </i>end up in one of the nicer parts of the Underworld, <i>and</i> leave some family members behind to make offerings that ensure you'll live comfortably. It'd <i>really suck</i> if your emergence into the lands of the dead was right in front of some of the nastier fauna or some spectral slaver, or if you just didn't know how to get by on what's around.*<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, your loved ones might wash up in a different part of the Underworld, or <i>not</i> continue on as a ghost, or get caught up in the machinations of one of the Deathlords. Them being dead doesn't mean you're going to necessarily stop worrying about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> __________________________<br /> *\u200bThe Underworld isn't <i>Minecraft</i> - a new arrival isn't necessarily going to be able to punch a tree to get materials to build tools to harvest materials to build things until he's created a grand civilization for himself; moreover, a lot of these places are already inhabited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-05-2021, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T12:13:52-07:00","id":1451070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451047#post1451047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean for many mortals in Creation being a ghost might be better than being alive. As a ghost you don't have to worry about starving to death, you don't have to worry about disease, you don't have to worry about droughts or natural disasters. You don't have to worry about getting older. You don't have to worry about dying. You don't have to worry about the people you care for dying. If you're a ghost you can spend eternity with your loved ones, largely free from pain or worries. In many respects, existing as a ghost (immortal, free from the pains of life, surrounded forever by the people you love) is not so different from the concept of Heaven that quite a few real-world religions preach about.<br /> <br /> To the the starving, the destitute, the diseased, the crippled, etc, the Underworld could look like a pretty attractive alternative than the continual suffering they experience daily in Creation. And of course, people could take the long-term view - if you're only going to live for 40 or 50 years and then exist as a ghost for half a million years after that, why feel too attached to those mere 50 years, especially if they mostly suck?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I find it extremely doubtful that when more details are given on what it is like to be a ghost that the answer is going to be 'exactly like being a mortal but even better because now you don't need to eat and don't age'. The fact that what we consider a ghost is only half of a two part soul in of itself kinda mandates that you aren't going to be the same as the living person whose self is a mixture of their higher and lower souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T17:20:38-07:00","id":1451086,"title":"","content":"I guess assessing ghosts depends on how one approaches certain information about the functions of the setting. Is it about figuring out an objective model of how things work and assessing characters and cultures on the basis of levels of ignorance, or about immersion in the values and priorities and extent of knowledge that can be felt by the characters?<br /> <br /> Sure enough, ghosts have to be lacking something vital to being alive because the general tone of the setting is that death has actual weight as a form of irreversible loss and there shouldn't really be an unambiguous sense that people are better off for having been killed. But at the same time, presenting ghosts as a means of bringing luxuries and experiences and a measure of power that would not have been possessed while alive, and that can shape a society in the form of ancestral cults and funereal practices, it makes the Underworld more compelling as a setting and way for it to engage with the living world, and so there's significance to how it's perceived on the ground level.<br /> <br /> Disagreements over these matters creates interesting character conflict. You can have Abyssals who are enemies of life because they've formed a conclusion that life sucks and the Underworld is preferable, and people at large need to be brought to this realisation whether they want to or not; Abyssals who come across as genuinely nice folks. You can have also Abyssals who are doing that whole thing about interceding on behalf of the dead and making sure the dead do right be the living sincerely, but really being crotchety unpleasant jerks as though go about it, because good ideals don't necessarily make for a good personality. Either of those can be opposed by a Solar whose concerns are less spiritual and more based on pragmatic territorial investment; people need to be alive for the sake of state revenues, which also benefit from not making expensive funerals or burnt offerings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T02:09:06-07:00","id":1451123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1450989#post1450989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hum...maybe. It could fit in both Infernal and Abyssal categories. I'm inclined more towards Infernal due to his background.</div> </div> </div> </div> Trust me, Guts is a perfect fit for a renegade Abyssal: a tortured wanderer, feared by those around him, dragging a pall of doom wherever he goes.<br /> <br /> <i>Femto</i> is the Infernal, brought to his life's nadir and raised to its zenith, a demon prince blind to anything but the realization of his dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:13:34-07:00","id":1451133,"title":"","content":"Excerpt from <i>The Graveyard Book</i>, by Neil Gaiman, Chapter 3: The Hounds of God...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bod said, \u201cI become one of you? You mean, I\u2019ll turn into you?\u201d<br /> \u201cSmart as a whip, sharp as a tack, you\u2019d have to get up pretty late at night to put anything past this lad,\u201d said the Bishop of Bath and Wells. \u201cIndeed. One of us. As strong, as fast, as unconquerable.\u201d<br /> \u201cTeeth so strong they can crush any bones, and tongue sharp and long enough to lick the marrow from the deepest marrowbone or flay the flesh from a fat man\u2019s face,\u201d said the Emperor of China.<br /> \u201cAble to slip from shadow to shadow, never seen, never suspected. Free as air, fast as thought, cold as frost, hard as nails, dangerous as, as us,\u201d said the Duke of Westminster.<br /> Bod looked at the creatures. \u201cBut what if I don\u2019t want to be one of you?\u201d he said.<br /> \u201cDon\u2019t want to? Of course you wants to! What could be finer? I don\u2019t think there\u2019s a soul in the universe doesn\u2019t want to be just like us.\u201d<br /> \u201cWe\u2019ve got the best city\u2014\u201d<br /> \u201cGh\u00fblheim,\u201d said the 33rd President of the United States.<br /> \u201cThe best life, the best food\u2014\u201d<br /> \u201cCan you imagine,\u201d interrupted the Bishop of Bath and Wells, \u201chow fine a drink the black ichor that collects in a leaden coffin can be? Or how it feels to be more important than kings and queens, than presidents or prime ministers or heroes, to be sure of it, in the same way that people are more important than brussels sprouts?\u201d<br /> Bod said, \u201cWhat are you people?\u201d<br /> \u201cGhouls,\u201d said the Bishop of Bath and Wells. \u201cBless me, somebody wasn\u2019t paying attention, was he? We\u2019re ghouls.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> \u201cI want to go home,\u201d said Bod, when the last of the bits in the song had been consumed. \u201cI don\u2019t want to be here.\u201d<br /> \u201cDon\u2019t take on so,\u201d said the Duke of Westminster. \u201cWhy, you little coot, I promise you that as soon as you\u2019re one of us, you\u2019ll not ever remember as you even had a home.\u201d<br /> \u201cI don\u2019t remember anything about the days before I was a ghoul,\u201d said the famous writer Victor Hugo.<br /> \u201cNor I,\u201d said the Emperor of China, proudly.<br /> \u201cNope,\u201d said the 33rd President of the United States.<br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll be one of a select band, of the cleverest, strongest, bravest creatures ever,\u201d bragged the Bishop of Bath and Wells. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:37:20-07:00","id":1451139,"title":"","content":"In earlier editions, ghosts weren't trapped in the Underworld or anything. If a ghost ever got tired of being a ghostm for whatever reason, they could always fall into Lethe and seek reincarnation pretty much whenever they wanted (mechanically if a ghost &quot;died&quot; they had to make a Willpower roll to avoid falling into Lethe, so a ghost who truly hated their existence could just choose to fail that roll and fall into Lethe at any time). Being a ghost was a struggle, in fact, one in which you had to resist the slow but constant pull of Lethe. The exception were Ghosts who had become sacrificial grave goods and were eternally bound to another ghost (I don't expect that concept to make a return in 3rd edition), but even then you had stuff like Lethe Serpent venom which could be used by a ghost to fall into Lethe if they are unable to do so on their own, for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> The Exalted Underworld was heavily based off of Wraith: The Oblivion, but there were big differences. In Wraith, being a wraith sucked hard. You had a Shadow constantly trying to turn you into a Spectre and a single moment of weakness and you were fucked up forever. Further, there was no &quot;escape&quot; from the Underworld. You couldn't fall into Lethe and get reincarnated. Transcendence was a myth so for most wraiths there were only one of two possible endings for them - either eventually becoming a Spectre after a Harrowing or eventually getting soulforged into Soulsteel. Every day was just trying to ignore one of those two eventual ends.<br /> <br /> But Exalted specifically did not work that way, so the Underworld and existence as ghosts were not such terrible things (worse than being alive in some ways, but also better in some other ways). The Underworld wasn't a trap or anything, and it was something ghosts could &quot;Nope&quot; out of if they truly did not want to be ghosts (but clearly lots and lots of ghosts didn't mind their continued existence). Of course, that could all change in 3rd edition, and the Underworld could end up as a horrible place that makes Wraith: The Oblivion look like a paradise for all we know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:54:56-07:00","id":1451141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451139#post1451139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In earlier editions, ghosts weren't trapped in the Underworld or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to get out of the Underworld, you'd need access to a shadowland. And unless you can convince someone in Creation to murder a whole bunch of people for you to open the way, chances are pretty decent that someone's already controlling it from one side or another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451139#post1451139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a ghost ever got tired of being a ghostm for whatever reason, they could always fall into Lethe and seek reincarnation pretty much whenever they wanted (mechanically if a ghost &quot;died&quot; they had to make a Willpower roll to avoid falling into Lethe, so a ghost who truly hated their existence could just choose to fail that roll and fall into Lethe at any time).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure you <i>had to</i> actually roll the dice, because if you botched you would be sucked into Oblivion instead.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, &quot;you can always choose to stop existing&quot; isn't exactly what I'd call a great way out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451139#post1451139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that could all change in 3rd edition, and the Underworld could end up as a horrible place that makes Wraith: The Oblivion look like a paradise for all we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've already been given glimpses of the Underworld for 3e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T07:59:58-07:00","id":1451142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451139#post1451139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exception were Ghosts who had become sacrificial grave goods and were eternally bound to another ghost (I don't expect that concept to make a return in 3rd edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T01:18:39-07:00","id":1451421,"title":"","content":"Taking into account the nature of Liminal exalted, does it mean that Abyssals and Liminals are automatic enemies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T03:35:01-07:00","id":1451426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451421#post1451421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking into account the nature of Liminal exalted, does it mean that Abyssals and Liminals are automatic enemies?</div> </div> </div> </div> We don't have much on the Liminal Exalted, but they don't exactly seem to have any organization. Just the &quot;silent impulses&quot; of their Dark Mother (and a powerset that is probably pretty good at fucking over the undead) to set them on the exorcist's path.<br /> <br /> They're still mostly individuals, though, as are the deathknights, so at a guess I'd say they are <i>natural</i> enemies rather than automatic ones: there's ready-made conflict there, but nothing on either side really keeping them from teaming up.<br /> For comparison, DBs, Sidereals, and Lunars all have formal organizations with centuries of bad blood and deliberate pogroms between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T12:27:12-07:00","id":1451561,"title":"","content":"The Guilty Gear series has Slayer, the vampiric founder of an assassin\u2019s guild. He\u2019s a noble philanthropist who loves the beauty of the human world despite knowing it\u2019s not truly his world. He\u2019s a solid example of the \u201cchivalry of death\u201d concept that Ex3/Essence Abyssals aim for.<br /> <br /> (It\u2019s worth noting that his vision of the Assassin\u2019s Guild as an altruistic opponent of evil is cheapened and made mercenary when he steps back from his leadership role.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 06-10-2021, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T15:12:32-07:00","id":1451760,"title":"","content":"I wonder is Spawn would be better as Infernal than Abyssal. I could see him as either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T10:03:08-07:00","id":1451871,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with an Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 06-12-2021, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T11:45:18-07:00","id":1451888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451871#post1451871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with am Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Solars are a &quot;new&quot; thing in Creation and, therefore, not prejudiced? Look at Moray Darktide in previous editions. He's a Solar working for a Deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>Inevitable Meerkat Style</b></i><br /> <i>The Student Sutra of Spotlight Hoging: Once, there was a maiden, but who cares about those? Let's talk about Lunars.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8863-slulura","name":"Slulura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8863_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T17:04:51-07:00","id":1451925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451871#post1451871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with an Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possessing a similar goal? Lust? Pity? Friendship? Any number of possible reasons really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T17:44:37-07:00","id":1451928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451871#post1451871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with an Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Solar won a duel, and everything escalated from there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T20:49:32-07:00","id":1452272,"title":"","content":"Three pages and no one mentions Vampire Hunter D? For shame.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://bloody-disgusting.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/vampire-hunter-d-bloodlist.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T02:01:14-07:00","id":1452293,"title":"","content":"D has some of the aesthetic and I think a comparable ability or two, but he doesn't quite reference the particulars of Abyssal narratives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T03:56:15-07:00","id":1452301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackwingedheaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1452272#post1452272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three pages and no one mentions Vampire Hunter D? For shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought my showing up a few pages back would be enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-16T06:52:25-07:00","id":1452469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451871#post1451871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with an Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my 3E game that I ran a while back, the Circle's Night Caste ended up finding out that the man she was betrothed to, before fleeing prior to their wedding, ended up exalting as a Dusk Caste who served Walker in Darkness. After a very tense meal, and a heartfelt apology for running away from the Night Caste, the Dusk ended up traveling with them for a bit, as they began to mess with Thorns and the Mask of Winters, which meant their goals aligned neatly and the rest of the group wasn't going to turn away a Dusk Caste Single Point stylist that wanted to come with them.<br /> <br /> The Dusk actually ended up being a valued member of the Circle, and he and the Night ended up restarting their relationship- the epilogue basically had the two of them going off together for more adventures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T04:08:32-07:00","id":1454338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451871#post1451871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with an Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my last Exalted game, there was an Abyssal tooling around with a bunch of Solars and a Lunar because the Lunar was his mate, and one of the Solars was his Circle-mate from a previous life. He wanted to escape the service of the Deathlords, and he needed a strong moral compass to keep him from defaulting to solving every problem with slaughter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />&quot;The true object of all human life is play. Earth is a task garden; heaven is a playground.&quot; -G.K. Chesterton","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/53-blackwingedheaven","name":"blackwingedheaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar53_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T19:32:55-07:00","id":1454408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451871#post1451871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with an Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Somewhere in the Neck:]<br /> <br /> Abyssal: \u201cWhat\u2019s the mistress of the magistrate who got me and my family executed doing here and why is she wearing 500 pounds of soulsteel OH GODS she saw me just play it cool.\u201d<br /> <br /> Solar: \u201cWhy is a dead girl with a probable grudge against my ex walking around in broad daylight OH NO she\u2019s coming this way just act natural.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then they got drinks, did some sympathizing for each other, and decided beggars can\u2019t be choosers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T12:48:08-07:00","id":1454542,"title":"","content":"Heroic Abyssals, as &quot;champions of death,&quot; are also strangely suited for &quot;Adventurer Archaeologist&quot; and Epic Historian characters: venerating the past over the present isn't so different from venerating the dead over the living.<br /> <br /> The necromantic proficiencies of Abyssals are also very useful for unearthing knowledge lost to the ages \u2013 interviewing ghosts, retrieving memories from past lives, calling forth phantasms of long-lost buildings and civilizations, etc. Breezing through ancient tombs to retrieve/protect burial goods from unscrupulous scavenger lords would also be very much in-character for a non-evil Abyssal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12641-aldosalt","name":"AldoSalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12641_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T14:10:57-07:00","id":1455040,"title":"","content":"To me a heroic abyssal is an exemplar of the belief that sometimes things must end and bad people gotta die, making them sort of counterparts to Endings sids. I can easily see an Abyssal from one of the realm's satrapies going around butchering the imperialists that crushed his homeland, which is...more heroic than Abyssals usually are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T14:36:04-07:00","id":1455129,"title":"","content":"I wonder what could be done with an Abyssal patterned after Death of the Endless:<br /> <hr /><br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_(DC_Comics)\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ec/Death_%28DC_Comics%29.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> I mean, death is something we all fear; but it doesn't <i>have</i> to be a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-18T19:42:42-07:00","id":1455157,"title":"","content":"Nobody's mentioned <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0001.html\" target=\"_blank\">Secret</a> yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T20:46:20-07:00","id":1455287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1455157#post1455157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody's mentioned <a href=\"https://keychain.patternspider.net/archive/koc0001.html\" target=\"_blank\">Secret</a> yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beat me to it. seriously, Keychain of creation's Secret is a prime example and imho should become canon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2610-lycaniz","name":"lycaniz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T13:01:10-07:00","id":1455585,"title":"","content":"I always thought <a href=\"https://www.shortoftheweek.com/2009/02/23/comedy/\" target=\"_blank\">Studio 4\u00b0C's <i>Comedy</i></a> was a good Abyssal inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T18:00:24-07:00","id":1455687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AldoSalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1454542#post1454542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroic Abyssals, as &quot;champions of death,&quot; are also strangely suited for &quot;Adventurer Archaeologist&quot; and Epic Historian characters: venerating the past over the present isn't so different from venerating the dead over the living.<br /> <br /> The necromantic proficiencies of Abyssals are also very useful for unearthing knowledge lost to the ages \u2013 interviewing ghosts, retrieving memories from past lives, calling forth phantasms of long-lost buildings and civilizations, etc. Breezing through ancient tombs to retrieve/protect burial goods from unscrupulous scavenger lords would also be very much in-character for a non-evil Abyssal</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of an Ars Magica character in one of the fanzines. A storyteller with the best stories, who got them by raising a corpse, asking them for their life story, and then sending them to lethe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T19:22:26-07:00","id":1455692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpoonR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1455687#post1455687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reminds me of an Ars Magica character in one of the fanzines. A storyteller with the best stories, who got them by raising a corpse, asking them for their life story, and then sending them to lethe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I have all of those fanzines. I have a hankering to look at that character, could you share with me which fanzine and issue so that I can examine him/her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T11:36:21-07:00","id":1455761,"title":"","content":"<br /> The classic example of a heroic abyssal is someone who has rebelled against their deathlord masters and seeks to redeem themselves, culminating in becoming a Solar.<br /> <br /> Otherwise being a heroic abyssal in Creation is like being a good-aligned vampire. It's not that it's *impossible*, you can *do* it, but everything about what you are is going to rail against it. It is your doom to fulfill the oath you made to the Neverborn, spread death across all of Creation and bring closer the ultimate triumph of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> But that's part of what makes Exalted interesting, innit? The game revolves around power, how best to use it, the inevitable corrupting influence it has.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your power is inherently destructive, corrupted and terrible for Creation in the long run, how do you use it to do good?&quot; is an immediately interesting question. You might act as a diplomat for the dead, negotiating deals to give the Underworld some semblance of order, or finding a way to help the ghosts in a shadowland coexist with the living until they can finally find a way to Lethe. You could be a monster hunter, tracking down hungry ghosts, mortwights and the like, ending them before they cause trouble. You could be a Punisher-style antihero, turning your unbridled, screaming NEED for destruction towards the dismantling of, say, the Realm, the slave trade or dinosaur heroine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T07:58:44-08:00","id":1528541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1450874-show-me-a-heroic-abyssal?p=1451871#post1451871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here's my following question \u00bfWhy would a Solar partner with an Abyssal, their literal opposites? I'm not looking for a definite answer, just examples based on your characters and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first week of being a Solar generally involves a whole shit load of people doing their level best to kill you before you can become <i>a Problem. </i>The weird gothy dude/chick/other who kills the people trying to kill you and talks you through this whole thing you're involved with makes a good a new friend as anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T06:32:40-08:00","id":1528644,"title":"","content":"Also, in Exalted there's no 'Detect Evil' spell. There's 'detect holy' and 'detect demonic' and 'detect necrotic', but no 'detect evil'. And if you wanna detect demon/ dead, you need the charm. So yes there's no real need for an abyssal and solar pair to be impossible, merely improbable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}